%I A249106 #35 Oct 11 2026 16:45:22
%S A249106 19164,129357,14971875,45316123,434325391,1102826289,3945594513
%N A249106 Numbers that form a Pythagorean 6-tuple with their first four arithmetic derivatives.
%C A249106 From _Carlo Corti_, Oct 05 2026: (Start)
%C A249106 For every prime p, 4791*p^p is a term, with first four arithmetic derivatives 6391*p^p, 7962*p^p, 14603*p^p, 15479*p^p and hypotenuse 24084*p^p (Corti, Theorem 3).
%C A249106 Equivalently, 4791*A051674(k) is a term for every k >= 1, so the sequence is infinite. This family does not include every term: the primes 2, 3, 5, 7 yield indices 1, 2, 3, 7, so the prime parameter does not determine the sequence index.
%C A249106 10^10 < a(8) <= 4791*11^11 = 1366928213897301. (End)
%H A249106 Carlo Corti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23155533">An Exact Extension and an Infinite Family for OEIS A249106</a>, Zenodo archive, 2026 (paper, code, data and validation).
%H A249106 Carlo Corti, <a href="/A249106/a249106.txt">Table of i, a(i), the first four arithmetic derivatives of a(i), and the integer root, for i = 1..7</a>
%H A249106 Victor Ufnarovski and Bo Åhlander, <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals/JIS/VOL6/Ufnarovski/ufnarovski.html">How to Differentiate a Number</a>, Journal of Integer Sequences 6 (2003), Article 03.3.4 (Theorems 4 and 6).
%e A249106 First four arithmetic derivatives of 19164 are 25564, 31848, 58412, 61916 and sqrt(19164^2 + 25564^2 + 31848^2 + 58412^2 + 61916^2) = 96336.
%p A249106 with(numtheory);
%p A249106 Dr:=proc(w) local x,p; x:=w*add(op(2,p)/op(1,p),p=ifactors(w)[2]); end:
%p A249106 P:=proc(q,h) local a,b,k,n; for n from 2 to q do a:=n; b:=n^2;
%p A249106 for k from 1 to h do a:=Dr(a); b:=b+a^2; od; if type(sqrt(b),integer) then print(n);
%p A249106 fi; od; end: P(10^9,4);
%Y A249106 Cf. A003415, A051674, A210503, A230543, A249105, A249107, A249110.
%K A249106 nonn,more
%O A249106 1,1
%A A249106 _Paolo P. Lava_, Oct 21 2014
%E A249106 a(4) from _Ray Chandler_, Dec 23 2016
%E A249106 a(5) from _Ray Chandler_, Jan 11 2017
%E A249106 a(6)-a(7) from _Carlo Corti_, Oct 05 2026
